1. **Attempt 2's regression explained**: replacing lateral acceptance ("subproblem min must not degrade") with strict full-min acceptance removed the basin-hopping power — lateral moves let the chain cross active-set basins so the *following* `_asan_round` rebalance can raise the full min; strict acceptance rarely fires directly. Keep the parent's lateral variant.

2. **Gain mechanism preserved and strengthened**: the leave-one-out exact 2-D re-placement stays intact; it now triggers every 5th perturbation trial instead of every 8th (mid-search, where the incumbent still has room to jump basins), and its terminal polish alternates both active-set solvers twice, so any relocation gets fully exploited before acceptance.

3. **Monotonicity & budget**: every accept is strictly monotone on the exact 165-triple min; added compute is one extra polish round per `_reinsert` call (milliseconds each) and ~11 more mid-search hop invocations — total eval time stays near the parent's 58 s, far under the 360 s limit.
